            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-11065",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/go-viper/mapstructure/v2: Go-viper's mapstructure May Leak Sensitive Information in Logs in github.com/go-viper/mapstructure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in github.com/go-viper/mapstructure/v2, in the field processing component using mapstructure.WeakDecode. This vulnerability allows information disclosure through detailed error messages that may leak sensitive input values via malformed user-supplied data processed in security-critical contexts."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-11065",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-11065\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/go-viper/mapstructure/v2\nFixed Version: 2.4.0\nLink: [CVE-2025-11065](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-11065)\nA flaw was found in github.com/go-viper/mapstructure/v2, in the field processing component using mapstructure.WeakDecode. This vulnerability allows information disclosure through detailed error messages that may leak sensitive input values via malformed user-supplied data processed in security-critical contexts.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-11065**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/go-viper/mapstructure/v2|2.4.0|[CVE-2025-11065](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-11065)|\n\nA flaw was found in github.com/go-viper/mapstructure/v2, in the field processing component using mapstructure.WeakDecode. This vulnerability allows information disclosure through detailed error messages that may leak sensitive input values via malformed user-supplied data processed in security-critical contexts."
